## Detail by document

### 2026-08-24 · HANDOVER_nameSortKey_import_fix.md
**Scope.** One-function fix unblocking the DDS4/BOH3 section of `main.ipynb`. `boh3_dds4_utils.py`
imports `nameSortKey` from `general_utils` (line 35) and calls it to order the entrustment
time-series PDF pages A–Z by surname (line 2491), but the function was **never defined** anywhere —
the code comment even says it should live in `general_utils`. Added it there (before `applyRosterOrder`).

- **`nameSortKey(name)`** — takes a single display-name string, returns a casefolded 2-tuple
  `(surname, firstName)`. Last whitespace token = surname, remainder = given name(s); handles
  `None`/blank → `("", "")`. Callers append the student number as the tie-breaker:
  `(*nameSortKey(name), number)`. Same surname heuristic as `boh2_dds2_dds3_utils._surnameKey`'s
  no-roster fallback, but a simpler signature (no roster map) matching this call site.
- **No notebook change.** The DDS4/BOH3 first cell now imports cleanly; behaviour is A–Z-by-surname
  page order (previously the file could not import at all).
- **Verification.** `py_compile` clean; unit spot-checks of the surname split + a case-insensitive
  sort demo. Not yet run end-to-end against live Postgres.
- **Caveat.** Surname = last token is a heuristic; compound/space-separated surnames may order on
  the wrong key (cosmetic page order only). Roster-accurate ordering would need a `rosterMap`
  threaded to this call site, as `orderStudentsBySurname` does.

